 "about_text": "Musichead Gallery is a Los Angeles gallery devoted to fine-art music photography, founded in 1998 by Detroit-born music entrepreneur Sam Milgrom, who previously ran the record store Sam's Jams and the live venue The Magic Bag before relocating to the West Coast. Located on Sunset Boulevard in Hollywood, the gallery represents more than eighty music photographers and offers vintage and contemporary prints spanning decades of rock, pop, jazz, and soul history, alongside in-house custom framing and art-consultancy services. Its rotating exhibitions have focused on individual artists and eras, from Miles Davis and Joni Mitchell to Oasis and Madonna, often drawing on photographers' archives and estates.",
